      "writtenOn": "2023-06-22T06:07:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Fun thoughs: timeToNextRun can be negative if the task didn\u0027t run exactly at the scheduled time, in which case it would be \u003c smallestRemainingTtl if there is no known TTL (smallestRemainingTtl \u003d\u003d 0).\n\ncalculateTimeToRunNextTasksInMsLocked / getSmallestRemainingTtlForExtensionLocked is a bit hard to follow. The second one would return 0 if there\u0027s no service, but also if a service is expired or about to expire, but these 2 cases should probably have different behavior.\n\nCould you have just one method that calculates the time for the next task ? Maybe something like:\n\n    calculateTimeToRunNextTasksInMsLocked(long now, QueryTaskConfig config)\n        --\u003e if (!config.shouldUseQueryBackoff) return now + config.timeWithoutBackoffMs\n        --\u003e If there is a service, and 0.8*minTtl \u003e timeWithoutBackoffMs, return now + 0.8*minTtl\n        --\u003e Otherwise return now + timeWithoutBackoffMs",
